# NestJS CRUD Pattern

When creating a new domain module, follow this structure:

```
src/<module>/
├── <module>.module.ts
├── <module>.controller.ts
├── <module>.service.ts
├── entities/
│   └── <module>.entity.ts
└── dto/
    ├── create-<module>.dto.ts
    └── update-<module>.dto.ts
```

## Controller

- Use `@ApiTags` and `@ApiBearerAuth` on protected routes
- CRUD paths use the `Methods` enum: `create`, `update/:id`, `delete/:id`
- List endpoints use `@PaginationHelper()` for query params
- Admin routes: `@RolesDecorator(...ADMIN_ROLES)`
- User routes: `@RolesDecorator(...USER_ROLES)` when applicable

## Service

- Inject `Repository<Entity>` via `@InjectRepository`
- Throw `NotFoundException` with i18n keys
- Pagination: `paginate()` from `nestjs-typeorm-paginate`

## Module

- Register entities with `TypeOrmModule.forFeature([Entity])`
- Export the service when other modules depend on it
- Register the module in `app.module.ts`

## Registration example

```typescript
@Module({
  imports: [TypeOrmModule.forFeature([Product])],
  controllers: [ProductController],
  providers: [ProductService],
  exports: [ProductService],
})
export class ProductModule {}
```
